    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Zero-downtime deployment strategies aim to update applications without service interruptions, but they create temporary states where multiple versions run simultaneously. For CORS, this means ensuring that all active versions-old and new-maintain compatible CORS policies throughout the deployment transition. A deployment that updates CORS configuration to add a new origin must ensure the configuration change is applied to all running instances before routing traffic that uses the new origin, otherwise some requests will be blocked by instances still running the old configuration."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
